  "id": "Compound::DB00503 - Gene::1577",
  "verbalization": "Ritonavir's relationship with Cyp3a5 is supported by multiple indirect pathways that converge through its role as an inducer of cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Ritonavir, through its inclusion in the Cytochrome P450 2c19 Inducers and Cytochrome P450 3a Inhibitors classes, indirectly influences Cyp3a5 expression. This is further reinforced by its binding to Cyp3a51p, which is part of the Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p complex, and its interaction with Rifapentine, an anti-infective agent that binds to Cyp3a5. The shared lowest common ancestors—Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound and Anti-Infective Agent—highlight a common functional role in drug metabolism and infection response. These pathways collectively suggest that Ritonavir modulates Cyp3a5 activity through enzyme induction or inhibition, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains partially inferred.",
